{
  "id": "u04-l03",
  "unit": "u04-food",
  "title": "I eat, you eat",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Here's your first full verb. The stem is **খা-** (*kha-*), and the ending shows who:\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| আমি / আমরা | **খাই** (*khai*) |\n| তুই | **খাস** (*khash*) |\n| তুমি | **খাও** (*khao*) |\n| আপনি / তিনি / উনি | **খান** (*khan*) |\n| সে / ও / তারা | **খায়** (*khay*) |\n\nNotice again: polite forms end in **-ন**, and polite 'you' = polite 'he/she'.\n\nBengali **eats** drinks: **আমি পানি খাই** = 'I drink water', **চা খাই** = 'I drink tea'. (Even cigarettes are 'eaten'!)\n\nTo say 'don't', put **না** *after* the verb: **আমি মাংস খাই না** = 'I don't eat meat.' The word order is subject – object – verb: আমি ভাত খাই = 'I rice eat.'",
  "vocab": [
